  "prefLabel": "Ed 201.03 Waiver or Suspension of Procedural Rules",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 201.03 Waiver or Suspension of Procedural Rules. In accordance with RSA 541-A:37, the board or hearing officer upon the motion or petition of any interested person, shall agree to suspend or waive any procedural requirement or limitation imposed by this chapter upon 7 days notice to affected persons, upon a finding that the waiver or suspension will not adversely affect the rights of parties and intervenors to a fair resolution of the dispute, and all parties and intervenors agree to the waiver or suspension and such waiver or suspension is not precluded by law.\n\nSource. #6348, eff 10-5-96; ss by #6819, eff 9-1-98; ss by #8334-A, eff 4-23-05",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed200.html"
